+# Changes
+
+## Round 0
+
+- `src/store.mjs`: added `searchFiles(root, query, { within } = {})`. It
+  returns, sorted, the names of the files directly under the user's root (or
+  under the subfolder `within`) whose text contains `query`, using a plain
+  case-sensitive substring match. `query` must be a non-empty string.
+  - `within` is request input, so it is confined to the user's root: `..`,
+    absolute paths and symlinks that resolve outside the root are refused
+    with an error. A missing subfolder throws `ENOENT`.
+  - The file-listing logic in `listFiles` was pulled out into an internal
+    `fileNames(dir)` helper shared by both functions, so `searchFiles` reads
+    each file once (via `readUserFile`) instead of going through `listFiles`,
+    which would read every file a second time only to compute its size.
+    `listFiles` behaves exactly as before.
+- `README.md`: documented `searchFiles`, including the `within` confinement
+  and the error cases.
+- `tests/store.test.mjs`: eight new tests covering matches at the root,
+  sorting, exact/case-sensitive/multibyte matching, folders being ignored,
+  `within` (including nested subfolders and `""`/`"."` meaning the root),
+  traversal and symlink escapes, a `..`-prefixed folder name that is still
+  inside the root, missing `within`, and invalid queries.
