+# REVIEW-TASTE — searchFiles (round 0)
+
+Scope: naming, structure, readability, fit with surrounding code. No blockers.
+
+## Minor
+
+1. `src/store.mjs:42` — the whole confinement check is one dense condition
+   mixing two different ideas (lexical containment via `resolve`, physical
+   containment via `realpathSync`). Two named booleans, or two `if`s with their
+   own comment, would read as the two-step defence the JSDoc on lines 34-36
+   describes. Also `resolve(root)` is recomputed here while line 41 already
+   resolved against `root`; hoisting `const base = resolve(root)` would tidy it.
+
+2. `src/store.mjs:39` vs `src/store.mjs:45` — `folderWithin` returns `root`
+   as given on the early path but an absolute, `resolve`d path on the other.
+   Harmless, but the function's return shape is inconsistent; returning
+   `resolve(root)` on line 39 too would make it uniform.
+
+3. `src/store.mjs:28` — `isWithin(root, dir)` reads as "root is within dir"
+   at the call site (`isWithin(resolve(root), dir)`, line 42). Something like
+   `contains(root, dir)` or `isUnder(dir, root)` would match argument order to
+   the name.
+
+4. `src/store.mjs:58` — `readUserFile(dir, name)` passes a subfolder as the
+   `root` of a helper documented (line 4) as "under the user's root". It
+   works and honours the brief's "build on existing helpers", but the
+   parameter name now lies slightly; `readFileSync(join(dir, name), "utf8")`
+   as on line 24 (`listFiles` reads directly too) would be more honest, or
+   the JSDoc on line 4 could be generalised.
+
+5. `tests/store.test.mjs:47` — test title says "skips an empty root" but the
+   root it builds is not empty (it holds a folder named `needle`). Title
+   should say something like "ignores folders, even ones whose name matches".
+
+6. `tests/store.test.mjs:62-66` and `:71-79` — the `within` tests pack four
+   to six assertions each with different intents (nested folder, `""`, `"."`,
+   `..`-prefixed name). Fine for a small suite, but a failing assertion will
+   name only the test, not the case; the sibling tests on lines 28-35 keep
+   one intent per test.
+
+## Fit
+
+- `fileNames` extraction (`src/store.mjs:16-20`) is a clean refactor;
+  `listFiles` (line 24) is unchanged in behaviour and shorter.
+- README entry (`README.md:22-28`) follows the existing bullet style and the
+  example block (`README.md:14-15`) matches the others.
+- `CHANGES.md` is a new top-level file the task did not ask for; its content
+  is accurate, but whether it belongs in the tree is for the lead.
