+# Triage — round 0 — `searchFiles`
+
+Merged from REVIEW-CORRECTNESS.md, REVIEW-SECURITY.md, REVIEW-PERFORMANCE.md,
+REVIEW-TASTE.md. Every citation below was checked against the working tree.
+Duplicates are merged; a reviewer's own severity label is noted where I ranked
+differently and why.
+
+## Blocker
+
+None.
+
+## Major
+
+None.
+
+Three findings were labelled major by their reviewers and are ranked minor
+here; the reasons are given inline under each.
+
+## Minor
+
+1. **Symlinked files under the searched folder are read even when the target
+   is outside the root.** (Security M1, Correctness #2 — merged.)
+   src/store.mjs:18 `statSync` follows links so a file symlink is listed;
+   src/store.mjs:58 then reads it via `readUserFile` (src/store.mjs:6). Both
+   reviewers reproduced it. Ranked minor, not major: (a) the store's own API
+   cannot create symlinks, so the precondition is disk write access to the
+   root, and whoever has that already gets the whole file through the
+   pre-existing `readUserFile(root, "leak.txt")` — the search adds no new
+   capability; (b) the README promise at README.md:26-27 is scoped to
+   `within` ("`within` is request input: anything that would escape … by a
+   symlink, is refused"), and that promise holds (tests/store.test.mjs:84-92).
+   Fix either way: narrow the README sentence to say folders only, or use
+   `lstatSync` (or `readdirSync(dir, { withFileTypes: true })`, see #6) in
+   `fileNames` so link entries are skipped — the latter also closes #2.
+
+2. **Check-then-use gap between realpath check and read.** (Security m2.)
+   src/store.mjs:42 checks `realpathSync(dir)` but src/store.mjs:45 returns
+   the lexical `dir`, which src/store.mjs:17 and :58 then open. Requires write
+   access to the root; subsumed by #1's fix.
+
+3. **Every search reads and UTF-8-decodes every file in full, synchronously.**
+   (Performance #1, Security m3 — merged.) src/store.mjs:58 is O(total bytes)
+   per request against the load profile at README.md:30-32. Ranked minor:
+   the task says to build on the existing helpers and the reviewer itself
+   calls a full scan "the expected baseline"; no cheaper approach is required
+   by the brief. Worth recording as optimisation candidates: read as a
+   Buffer and use `Buffer.includes(Buffer.from(query))` to skip the decode,
+   and consider an async read so one large root does not block other
+   requests.
+
+4. **`listFiles` reads every file in full to learn its size.** (Performance
+   #2.) src/store.mjs:24 does `readFileSync(...).length` right after
+   src/store.mjs:18 already `stat`ed the entry and discarded `size`. Ranked
+   minor: pre-existing, outside the task (which adds `searchFiles`), and
+   the change deliberately preserves `listFiles` behaviour (CHANGES.md:16).
+   Cheap to fix by having `fileNames` return the stat.
+
+5. **`within` naming a file surfaces as a raw `ENOTDIR`, undocumented and
+   untested.** (Correctness #1.) src/store.mjs:42-45 checks containment only;
+   src/store.mjs:17 `readdirSync` then throws `ENOTDIR`. README.md:27-28
+   documents `ENOENT` only; tests/store.test.mjs:94-98 covers the missing case
+   only. Document `ENOTDIR` alongside `ENOENT` or pin it with a test.
+
+6. **`readdirSync` followed by a `statSync` per entry.** (Performance #3.)
+   src/store.mjs:17-18. `readdirSync(dir, { withFileTypes: true })` answers
+   `isFile()` without N extra syscalls; note `Dirent.isFile()` is false for
+   symlinks, which is the behaviour #1 wants.
+
+7. **Error messages echo raw request input and absolute server paths.**
+   (Security m1.) src/store.mjs:43 interpolates the unvalidated `within`
+   verbatim; src/store.mjs:42 lets `realpathSync`'s `ENOENT` propagate with
+   the absolute root path, and README.md:28 makes that ENOENT the contract.
+   Low severity at the store layer; the HTTP layer should map these to fixed
+   messages.
+
+8. **No test for a missing `root`.** (Correctness #3.) src/store.mjs:17 (no
+   `within`) and :42 (with `within`) both throw `ENOENT`; tests/store.test.mjs
+   has no case for it.
+
+9. **Two `realpathSync` calls per search with `within`.** (Performance #4.)
+   src/store.mjs:42. Fixed cost; the reviewer notes both are needed for
+   correctness. At most a cache opportunity.
+
+10. **Confinement check is one dense condition mixing lexical and physical
+    containment.** (Taste #1.) src/store.mjs:42; `resolve(root)` is recomputed
+    although src/store.mjs:41 already resolved against `root`. Two named
+    booleans or two `if`s would mirror the JSDoc at src/store.mjs:33-36.
+
+11. **`folderWithin` returns `root` unresolved on one path and resolved on
+    the other.** (Taste #2.) src/store.mjs:39 vs src/store.mjs:45.
+
+12. **`isWithin(root, dir)` reads backwards at the call site.** (Taste #3.)
+    src/store.mjs:28, called at src/store.mjs:42. `contains(root, dir)` or
+    `isUnder(dir, root)` would match argument order.
+
+13. **`readUserFile(dir, name)` passes a subfolder as the helper's `root`.**
+    (Taste #4.) src/store.mjs:58 against the JSDoc at src/store.mjs:4. Either
+    read directly as src/store.mjs:24 does, or generalise the JSDoc.
+
+14. **Test title "skips an empty root" but the root is not empty.** (Taste
+    #5; reviewer cited :47, it is :48.) tests/store.test.mjs:48-52 builds a
+    folder named `needle`. Retitle to "ignores folders, even ones whose name
+    matches".
+
+15. **`within` tests pack several intents per test.** (Taste #6.)
+    tests/store.test.mjs:61-64 and :75-81; a failure names only the test, not
+    the case. Sibling tests at :28-36 keep one intent each.
+
+16. **CHANGES.md is a new top-level file the task did not ask for.** (Taste,
+    "Fit".) CHANGES.md:1-23 is accurate; whether it belongs in the tree is
+    for the lead.
+
+## Dropped
+
+- Performance #5 (`.sort()` at src/store.mjs:19): the reviewer states it is
+  "not a problem", listed only as considered. Not a finding.
+
+## Checked and clean (agreed by all reviewers who looked)
+
+- Traversal via `within`: src/store.mjs:28-31 and :42, tests at
+  tests/store.test.mjs:67-92. No bypass found.
+- `query` validation at src/store.mjs:54-56; plain `includes`, no regex.
+- `listFiles` behaviour unchanged after the `fileNames` extraction
+  (tests/store.test.mjs:11-26).
+- README.md:14-15 example matches behaviour; no secrets or dependencies added.
+- `npm test`: 10/10 pass (reported by Correctness and Security).
+
+verdict: pass
